    "body": "For example, users will undoubtedly attempt to convert `\"audio/ogg\"` to `\"audio/mp3\"` or `\"image/jpg\"` to `\"image/png\"` using `toDataURL()`. The processor itself should be capable of determining the correct MIME type of the input - or if the input is not possible of being converted into a valid `data URI`; for example, a media fragment URI which is capable of being played at an `HTMLMediaElement`, though does not contain the necessary metadata to be played after converting to a valid `data URI`.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fetch/issues/comments/361332671/reactions",
